    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear offensive anchor. His score of 82.13 is driven by a premier matchup against Ober, where a combination of a favorable wind and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014the most critical asset for our 5x5 construction. Joining him in the elite tier are **Christian Yelich** (72.74) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30). **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage against Alcantara, while **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a soft landing against Kay, benefiting from a high-leverage lineup spot that ensures maximum RBI opportunities.\n\nStrategic lineup construction relies heavily on capitalizing on the porous matchups against Merrill Kelly, elevating the profiles of **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Nelson Velazquez** (61.10). While **Yordan Alvarez** (59.18) remains a high-floor play, his score is slightly suppressed by the challenge of facing Kremer, an elite-level arm (3.23 xERA) compared to our other targets. Among the bench, **Casey Schmitt** (42.15) was the final player excluded from the starting nine; while he possesses strong platoon equity, his efficiency is neutralized by a difficult matchup against Miller, ultimately falling below the requisite threshold to displace **Luke Raley** or **Caleb Durbin**.\n\nManagement notes several situational risks today, primarily the \"Lineup Pending\" status of **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Nelson Velazquez**. Should these players shift lower in their respective batting orders, their daily efficiency scores will be subject to revision. We are avoiding exposure to **Chase Meidroth** entirely as he falls well below our 40.0 floor, and we continue to monitor the minor league status of **Hyeseong Kim** while **Trea Turner** remains sidelined during his scheduled off-day.",
